    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by the dual-threat upside of **Corbin Carroll** (81.86), whose leadoff assignment against Michael King provides an elite scoring environment. While King is a competent arm, the opportunity for **Corbin Carroll** to leverage his stolen base potential against a favorable matchup makes him our strongest play, bolstered by a 10% premium for his top-of-the-order role. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (75.06) is a vital cog today; he benefits from a generous SP_xERA of 4.95 from Bubba Chandler, and his efficiency is further compounded by a 4% boost for facing a pitcher with a slow delivery, significantly increasing his probability of padding our league-leading stolen base count.\n\nThe most difficult decision was managing our outfield depth against the left-handed starter Ian Seymour. **Mickey Moniak** (52.91) barely cleared the floor threshold; while the park factor in his favor is high (+14%), the aggressive negative platoon shift (-15%) against the lefty starter nearly forced his exclusion. However, because our other options like **Josh Naylor** and **Austin Riley** are sidelined by team off-days, and with **Trevor Story** and **Giancarlo Stanton** lingering on the IL, we are thin on high-ceiling utility pivots. **Jose Caballero** (57.32) remains in the lineup despite the order demotion and platoon disadvantage, as his baserunning upside is too high to bench in a 5x5 format where steals are the premium currency.\n\nWe are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **James Wood**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Corbin Carroll**. Any late-scratch shifts, particularly for **James Wood**\u2014who boasts an elite xwOBA of 0.422\u2014could disrupt our scoring floor. We continue to monitor the status of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot-start opportunities should the weather or confirmed lineups force a pivot away from our primary projections.",
